WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Prudhoe Bay, on Alaska's North Slope.

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.590
Oil was discovered here in 1968.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.530
Gravel roads now cross the flat tundra.

4
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.170
Beside them, road dust and roadside
flooding are helping frozen ground to thaw.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.710
Far to the south, Antarctica drew a few
hundred tourists a summer in the early

6
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.090
1990s.

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.950
Now it draws over 100,000 a year.

8
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.350
Badly built roads?

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.530
Or something about the cold itself?

10
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.930
Why are cold places so easily harmed?

11
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.470
In this mission, you'll trace
human impacts over time,

12
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.870
from whaling to oil to tourism, at local,

13
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.570
regional and ocean-wide scales.

14
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.470
Then you'll judge how cold
places are managed now,

15
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.510
and test that against possible futures.

16
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.960
Your mission: explain why cold
places are so easily harmed.
